25:/// editor owns [TableFloatingToolbarOverlayHost], which renders this payload with
26:/// Flutter's system [OverlayPortal] plus [CompositedTransformFollower]. This
27:/// keeps the toolbar outside the table block's internal [Stack], so it can cross
28:/// parent bounds and participate in overlay hit testing without making renderers
29:/// manage overlay entries directly.
